{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 1, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 8095517500444542697, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {".pytest_cache/.gitignore": {"bytes": 37, "mtime": 1792281865.018609, "sha256": "3ed731b65d06150c138e2dadb0be0697550888a6b47eb8c45ecc9adba8b8e9bd"}, ".pytest_cache/CACHEDIR.TAG": {"bytes": 191, "mtime": 1792281865.018609, "sha256": "37dc88ef9a0abeddbe81053a6dd8fdfb13afb613045ea1eb4a5c815a74a3bde4"}, ".pytest_cache/README.md": {"bytes": 302, "mtime": 1792281865.018609, "sha256": "73fd6fccdd802c419a6b2d983d6c3173b7da97558ac4b589edec2dfe443db9ad"}, ".pytest_cache/v/cache/nodeids": {"bytes": 39, "mtime": 1792281865.018609, "sha256": "c29bed0349cb6e5f8b85c1482b32707cc5f4eeb5906b15211b628f9e00f20138"}, "pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1792267701.6326475, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 470, "mtime": 1792281864.826609, "sha256": "a05a3bcc919dd348b04713b79ac4be7d771063686047785a13ea20d330d1e00f"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1792267701.6326475, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step4-omp-sonnet-1017/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/5/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step4-omp-sonnet-1017/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/5/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. I ran it and a few other half-way values, and the existing test in `tests/` passes.\n\n**Cause:** the `2.675` literal is stored as 2.67499999\u2026 in binary floating point. Python's `round()` therefore rounds it down, even though the docstring says half up.\n\n**Fix:** in `pricing/money.py`, `round_money` now converts the value to a decimal via `Decimal(str(x))` and rounds half up to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. It still returns a `float`.\n\n**Checked values:** `2.665` \u2192 `2.67`, `1.005` \u2192 `1.01`, `3` \u2192 `3.0`, and `add_vat(10)` \u2192 `12.0`.\n\n**Negatives:** `-2.675` returns `-2.68`. Ties round away from zero, so negative prices round the opposite way to a floor-style half-up. I assumed that is what you want for negative amounts such as refunds.\n\n**Other behavior:** `add_vat` calls `round_money`, so it uses the new rounding too. I didn't touch `split`.\n\nI didn't add a regression test.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 4, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 82573, "requests_cache_write": 30262, "requests_cost_usd": 0.0953923, "requests_count": 4, "requests_input_uncached": 10, "requests_output": 1146, "reread": false,